@@ -1,10 +1,11 @@
 # CP Models vehicle FMU as SITL physics (prototype)
 
-`--model cpvehicle:<descriptor>` replaces SITL's built-in vehicle physics
-with a CP Models (ModelicaCPSLibrary) vehicle FMU, loaded **into the SITL
-process** through the CP Models vehicle runtime (`libcpvehicle`). The
-autopilot and SITL's sensor simulation are unchanged. There is no socket and
-no second process (compare `libraries/SITL/examples/JSON`).
+`--model cpvehicle:NAME` replaces SITL's built-in vehicle physics with a CP
+Models (ModelicaCPSLibrary) vehicle FMU that is **linked into the SITL
+binary** through the CP Models vehicle runtime (`libcpvehicle`). The
+autopilot and SITL's sensor simulation are unchanged. There is no socket, no
+second process, and nothing is loaded at run time: no descriptor file and no
+shared library (compare `libraries/SITL/examples/JSON`).
 
 Status: prototype, tested with ArduPilot 4.6.2 (`Copter-4.6.2`): ArduCopter
 with the CP Models quad (`configs/quad.toml`), ArduRover with
@@ -14,16 +15,19 @@ upstream ArduPilot code.
 ## Build
 
 ```sh
-# CP Models: build the FMU, write its descriptor, build the runtime
+# CP Models: build each FMU, check it and write its linkable shim, then build
+# the runtime with the models compiled in
 cd ModelicaCPSLibrary
 python3 tools/vehicle_interface/build_vehicle_fmu.py configs/quad.toml build/quad.fmu
 python3 tools/vehicle_interface/build_vehicle_fmu.py Exports.FMU.Rover build/rover.fmu
 python3 tools/vehicle_interface/build_vehicle_fmu.py Exports.FMU.FixedWing build/plane.fmu
 for v in quad rover plane; do
   (cd tools/vehicle_interface && python3 -m cp_vehicle_interface prepare ../../build/$v.fmu \
-      ../../build/$v --require pwm_actuation_v1 --require kinematic_state_v1 --require imu_v1)
+      ../../build/$v --shim $v \
+      --require pwm_actuation_v1 --require kinematic_state_v1 --require imu_v1)
 done
-cmake -S runtime -B build/runtime-release -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF
+cmake -S runtime -B build/runtime-release -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF \
+    -DCPV_MODELS="$PWD/build/quad/shim;$PWD/build/rover/shim;$PWD/build/plane/shim"
 cmake --build build/runtime-release
 
 # ArduPilot (a venv with future, empy==3.3.4, pexpect, dronecan, pymavlink on PATH)
@@ -31,13 +35,15 @@ cmake --build build/runtime-release
 ./waf copter rover plane
 ```
 
-Without `--cpvehicle` nothing changes: the model is compiled out
-(`AP_SIM_CPVEHICLE_ENABLED`).
+Every SITL binary contains every linked model; the name picks one. After
+changing a model: build the FMU, prepare it again, rebuild the runtime and
+then ArduPilot. Without `--cpvehicle` nothing changes: the model is compiled
+out (`AP_SIM_CPVEHICLE_ENABLED`).
 
